// Grammar for the consumer-lane unparser/formatter smoke targets.
//
// Deliberately tiny, like the other consumer grammars: this lane's job is the cross-module
// path from `generate_rust_parser(unparser = True)` to a linked, running unparser, not
// generator breadth.
//
// It does need one thing consumer.fltkg lacks — a rule whose items the format spec can put
// spacing between — or rendering could not differ from the input text and the round-trip
// test would pass on a formatter that did nothing.

sum := lhs:num , "+" , rhs:num ;

num := value:/[0-9]+/ ;
